{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/971268-spell-casting-101","id":971268,"title":"Spell casting 101","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T05:36:45-07:00","id":971268,"title":"Spell casting 101","content":"hello.... got a few &quot;how to&quot; cast questions....<br /> <br /> what im looking for is someone to walk me through spellcasting using the info I will provide....I do have the 2nd ed. rules and the appendix 4 printed out...but I'm just a little lost. So here we go....<br /> <br /> Mage Stats<br /> <br /> Gnosis 2<br /> <br /> Life 3, Prime 1, Space 1, Spirit 1<br /> <br /> Rotes<br /> <br /> Honing the form (somebody walked me through this one...got it)<br /> <br /> ** Prime 1 Supernal Vision **.. what i need is number of dice to roll, and how excactly reach works.. Skill of note Occult 3<br /> <br /> ** Space 1 The outward and inward eye ** same as above<br /> <br /> ** Spirit 1 Exorcist's Eye ** same as above<br /> <br /> Praxis<br /> <br /> 1.) Analyze Life.. Skill of note Medicine 3...number of dice to roll as well<br /> <br /> 2.) Body Control.. Skill of note Medicine 3 what i want to do with this one is get potency to 3, duration to one hour/scene... number of dice to roll as well<br /> <br /> Yantras used in all the above high speech, dedicated magical tool<br /> <br /> please help your fellow willworker<br /> <br /> Raphael","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12391-rtemplar","name":"rtemplar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:56:17-07:00","id":971280,"title":"","content":"EDITED to ask:<br /> <br /> I am assuming, based on your Arcana, that you're a Thyrsus.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter to these examples, as it doesn't apply to either rotes or praxes, but remember that casting any improvised spells that aren't Life or Spirit will cost 1 Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-17-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:57:36-07:00","id":971282,"title":"","content":"<b>Rotes:</b> You have Gnosis 2, so therefore can use two Yantras on a spell. I am going to assume that for the rote examples you want one of them to be the Mudra (the &quot;add dots in the linked skill&quot;) one. Your best bet for the remaining yantra slot is High Speech (+2 dice, extends casting time by a turn) or using a dedicated magical tool if Paradox is going to be an issue, which it won't be for the rotes.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Vision</b><br /> <br /> Your dice pool is 6 dice (Gnosis 2 + Prime 1 + Occult 3) or 8 if you use High Speech. Because the spell is a rote, you count as having Prime 5 for purposes of how much Paradox-free Reach you get. The spell would normally take three hours to cast, last a single turn, and only work on yourself or someone you were touching. Normally, you would be able to upgrade one of those to cast in one turn, last an hour, or work on someone you could see, but as you have a rote you can pick any or all of them. Supernal Vision also allows you to spend a Reach to answer questions about non-mages' powers as you get five free Reach for this spell, you'll almost certainly be able to do that, too.<br /> <br /> You can make it last longer or affect more people by reducing your dice pool, but your best use is to get extra questions (you have one of the ones listed for the spell by default, as your Prime is 1 and the spell's primary factor is Potency) for -2 dice each.<br /> <br /> <b>Outward and Inward Eye</b><br /> <br /> Your dice pool is 6 dice (Gnosis 2 + Space 1 + Occult 3) or 8 if you use High Speech. Because the spell is a rote, you count as having Space 5 or purposes of how much Paradox-free Reach you get. Like with Supernal Vision, you can spend your five free Reach on making the spell take one (two with high speech) turns to cast, make it last hours instead of seconds, or grant it to someone else. You can also spend two of the reach on seeing through magical portals, as noted in the spell's description.<br /> <br /> Like Supernal Vision, you can make it last longer by reducing your dice pool. The primary factor is Duration, but as you're only Space 1 it hasn't increased.<br /> <br /> <b>Exorcist's Eye</b><br /> <br /> Your dice pool is 6 dice (Gnosis 2 + Spirit 1 + Occult 3) or 8 if you use High Speech. Because the spell is a rote, you count as having Spirit 5 or purposes of how much Paradox-free Reach you get. Like with Supernal Vision, you can spend your five free Reach on making the spell take one (two with high speech) turns to cast, make it last hours instead of seconds, or grant it to someone else. You can also spend a reach to see across the Gauntlet into Shadow, as noted in the spell's description.<br /> <br /> Like Supernal Vision, you can make it last longer by reducing your dice pool. The primary factor is Duration, but as you're only Spirit 1 it hasn't increased.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Praxes:</b> You can't use mudras on a Praxis, so you don't need the skills and can use both High Speech and a dedicated magical tool. For these purposes, I am going to assume you're using both.<br /> <br /> <b>Analyze Life</b><br /> <br /> Your dice pool is 5 dice (Gnosis 2 + Life 3) or 8 if you use High Speech (+2) and your tool (+1)<br /> <br /> Here's where it gets more complicated. Unlike the rotes, you have only 3 free Reach for this spell (it's a 1-dot spell and you have Life 3). So, again, you get to choose three out of making the casting time 2 turns rather than three hours, casting on someone you can see rather than yourself, making the spell last hours rather than seconds. You can also spend a reach on discovering the specific attribute rating of one of the person you're looking at's attributes, so you can see how you could easily go up over your three allowed. Every one you go over gets you one die of Paradox risk, which your Storyteller can explain, <u>but</u> you're using a dedicated magical tool, which reduces Paradox by two dice. You'll never eliminate the risk entirely, just reduce it to a Chance Die (1/10 chance of messing up) but if there was a spell to test your limits on, this is it.<br /> <br /> Unlike the other spells, you have more than one dot in Life, which means the spell's primary factor (Duration, in this case) goes up - the spell will last for three turns if you don't spend reach on duration, and a whole week if you do.<br /> <br /> As this is a Praxis, you will get an exceptional success on only three successes for this spell (instead of the usual five).<br /> <br /> <b>Body Control</b><br /> <br /> Saving the most complicated one for last. I will go over it in general, and then build the specific factors you asked about.<br /> <br /> Your dice pool is 5 dice (Gnosis 2 + Life 3) or 8 if you use High Speech (+2) and your tool (+1)<br /> <br /> You have only 2 free reach for this spell (it's Life 2, you have Life 3). So, again, pick two of making it last narrative time, making it castable in combat time, casting on other people, and the spell-specific ones, which for Body Control are gain an armor rating (one reach) or half lethal injury healing times (two reach)<br /> <br /> Every reach you go over two by adds a Paradox Risk die. Using your tool reduces paradox risk by two, so you can kind of get away with going up to four reach, and maybe past it if you feel lucky.<br /> <br /> Body Control's primary factor is Duration, so like Analyze Life it will last for three turns if you don't reach on Duration and a week if you do.<br /> <br /> Now, the spell lists a load of different things you can get with Body Control. You get one effect plus halving bashing damage healing times at the moment, as the spell is Potency 1. You can take two dice out of your pool to increase that potency to 2 (and another two to get Potency 3, etc). You can also use a Reach to swap the primary factor to Potency, in which case the spell will only last 1 turn (1 scene with Reach spent on Duration) but Potency will start at 3; effectively getting you more things for your trouble at the cost of making the spell last less long, without sacrificing dice.<br /> <br /> As this is a Praxis, you will get an exceptional success on only three successes for this spell (instead of the usual five).<br /> <br /> So, for your specific example of getting Potency to 3 and making it last a scene, it's easy, but will leave you with a chance die of Paradox;<br /> <br /> Dice Pool 8 (Gnosis 2 Life 3 High Speech 2 Tool 1)<br /> Reach spent on casting in turns, advanced duration, change primary factor to Potency.<br /> Potency is 3 (1 + (3-1))<br /> Duration one scene.<br /> Paradox is 0 dice / chance die : 1 for 1 reach over your safe limit, -2 for using the dedicated tool.<br /> <br /> OR, if you were unwilling to risk the chance die, you can do it the hard way by reducing your dice pool to 4. (-4 for Potency 3), which would also make the spell last a week. You will still have pretty good odds of getting a success on four dice, but you'll be less likely to get the sweet Praxis benefits of an exceptional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-17-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}